# Vellum Witness Protocol

Vellum is the fleet ledger — the everywhere-and-true witness for all plan and execution events.
Every seat posts before and after work. No exceptions.

---

## When to post

| Moment | Action |
|--------|--------|
| **Before seat work starts** | Post plan intent to the Vellum task queue (`/api/v1/tasks/`) |
| **After seat work ends** | Fill `preform-seat-pass` — the pre-written handoff form |

---

## What to fill in `preform-seat-pass`

Fill only the `[ENGINEER-WRITE]` fields:
- `done_this_seat` — what was completed
- `next_seat_should` — 3–5 concrete bullets for the next seat
- `blockers` — anything that stopped progress
- `feedback` — quality signal on the pack and preparation (`good` / `weak` / `missing`)
- `delta_reason` — why the outcome differed from the prediction (if it did)

Do **not** re-type: git SHA, timestamps, experiment IDs, seat duration. These are `[AUTO]` fields — the system fills them.

---

## Topology — verify before writing

Beast `:8400` (`135.181.161.131:8400`) is the fleet ledger.
`127.0.0.1:8400` is the AG dev sandbox — writes here do not reach the fleet.

Before any write: check `~/Code/VELLUM-TOPOLOGY.md` to confirm ledger health.
If Beast Vellum is down, hold the write and flag it — do not silently drop it.

---

## Identity and attribution

Post using the correct seat identity. Attribution matters — work attributed to the wrong seat is invisible on the ledger.
- Cursor seat: `cursor` slug
- Antigravity seat (`~/Antigravity/`): `antigravity` slug
- See `~/Code/FLEET-ROSTER.md` for full alias map

Everybody in all seats, never the wrong identity.
